<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh to import wheat under Japanese aid.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh to import wheat under Japanese aid.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh has tendered to buy Australian, Canadian or U.S. wheat under a 850 million yen Japanese food aid for shipment by February 24, government and Japanese embassy officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>Food ministry officials said bidding would take place at 0630 GMT on January 25. However, they would not specify the quantity of the wheat.</p>
<p>The embassy officials said the Japanese government offered the money as a grant to import the wheat under an agreement signed on November 19.</p>
</text>
